From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreyk <dreyksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt76x02: skip idle queues in TX cleanup

During 5 GHz TX NAPI polling on MT7612E, mt76x02_poll_tx() cleans the MCU
ring and data queues MT_TXQ_PSD..0 both before and after
napi_complete_done(). Most of those scans find an empty queue
(q->queued == 0), yet each call executes a PCIe MMIO read of the DMA
index register (~1.35 us CPU stall per read on MT7628AN).

Add bit 0 (MT76X02_TX_OPT_SKIP_IDLE, 1) to the module parameter tx_opt
of mt76x02_lib (on by default). When set, mt76x02_clean_tx_queue() skips
mt76_queue_tx_cleanup() if READ_ONCE(q->queued) == 0. The parameter is
read with READ_ONCE() on every call so writes take effect at run time
without reloading the module.

Waiters on dev->tx_wait check their pending condition before sleeping,
and any queue that held frames still runs mt76_queue_tx_cleanup() and
wakes waiters when it drains to empty. The pass-2 race around
napi_complete_done() stays closed: if frames were queued before pass 2,
q->queued is non-zero so pass 2 cleans them; later completions arrive
after interrupts are re-enabled.

Paired with skipping the catch-up DMA index re-read on MT7612E,
router-to-client UDP throughput rose +6.5% (23.1 vs 21.7 Mbit/s) and
90 Mbit/s TCP download gained +1.7 percentage points CPU idle (-1.3% CPU
per Mbit/s). In a 24.58-hour site run with all four tx_opt bits active
and an active-traffic channel-switch test (52->36->52: 4 switches with
the bits on and 4 without, same result in both), TX status timeouts
were 0.082% vs 0.093% without the patches, with zero TX hangs, zero
resets, and all 8 switches finishing in 1.83-2.02 s.

Writing 0 to the mt76x02_lib module parameter tx_opt restores the stock
behaviour.
---
 mt76x02.h      |  4 ++++
 mt76x02_mmio.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt76x02.h b/mt76x02.h
index 0d13dfa2..dac2869a 100644
--- a/mt76x02.h
+++ b/mt76x02.h
@@ -149,6 +149,10 @@ struct mt76x02_dev {
 	ktime_t ed_time;
 };
 
+#define MT76X02_TX_OPT_SKIP_IDLE		BIT(0)
+#define MT76X02_TX_OPT_DEFAULT			MT76X02_TX_OPT_SKIP_IDLE
+
+extern unsigned int tx_opt;
 extern struct ieee80211_rate mt76x02_rates[12];
 
 int mt76x02_init_device(struct mt76x02_dev *dev);
diff --git a/mt76x02_mmio.c b/mt76x02_mmio.c
index 8b9d5f86..4ec78683 100644
--- a/mt76x02_mmio.c
+++ b/mt76x02_mmio.c
@@ -23,6 +23,14 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(delay_int,
 #define MT76X02_DELAY_INT_EN		BIT(15)
 #define MT76X02_DELAY_INT_TX_SHIFT	16
 
+/* Bitmask of 5 GHz TX path optimizations (see MT76X02_TX_OPT_*). Read at
+ * run time; 0 restores stock behaviour.
+ */
+unsigned int tx_opt = MT76X02_TX_OPT_DEFAULT;
+module_param(tx_opt, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(tx_opt,
+		 "5 GHz TX path optimizations (bitmask): 1=skip idle queues; 0: off; default 0x1");
+
 /* The interrupt of the main RX ring; the MCU ring keeps its own */
 static u32 mt76x02_rx_main_int(struct mt76x02_dev *dev)
 {
@@ -177,6 +185,18 @@ static void mt76x02_tx_worker(struct mt76_worker *w)
 	mt76_txq_schedule_all(&dev->mphy);
 }
 
+static void mt76x02_clean_tx_queue(struct mt76x02_dev *dev, struct mt76_queue *q)
+{
+	if (!q)
+		return;
+
+	if ((READ_ONCE(tx_opt) & MT76X02_TX_OPT_SKIP_IDLE) &&
+	    !READ_ONCE(q->queued))
+		return;
+
+	mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev, q, false);
+}
+
 static int mt76x02_poll_tx(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget)
 {
 	struct mt76x02_dev *dev = container_of(napi, struct mt76x02_dev,
@@ -185,16 +205,16 @@ static int mt76x02_poll_tx(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget)
 
 	mt76x02_mac_poll_tx_status(dev, false);
 
-	mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev, dev->mt76.q_mcu[MT_MCUQ_WM], false);
+	mt76x02_clean_tx_queue(dev, dev->mt76.q_mcu[MT_MCUQ_WM]);
 	for (i = MT_TXQ_PSD; i >= 0; i--)
-		mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev, dev->mphy.q_tx[i], false);
+		mt76x02_clean_tx_queue(dev, dev->mphy.q_tx[i]);
 
 	if (napi_complete_done(napi, 0))
 		mt76x02_irq_enable(dev, mt76x02_tx_done_int(dev));
 
-	mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev, dev->mt76.q_mcu[MT_MCUQ_WM], false);
+	mt76x02_clean_tx_queue(dev, dev->mt76.q_mcu[MT_MCUQ_WM]);
 	for (i = MT_TXQ_PSD; i >= 0; i--)
-		mt76_queue_tx_cleanup(dev, dev->mphy.q_tx[i], false);
+		mt76x02_clean_tx_queue(dev, dev->mphy.q_tx[i]);
 
 	mt76_worker_schedule(&dev->mt76.tx_worker);
 
